  "primary": "Per-block sqrt(ab*ba)/auto ratios: ASCII median lower bound >1.05; Unicode >.99; other four >.98. One-sided exact order-statistic bounds at alpha=.05/6; outer block is the only replicate. Success requires ALL SIX bounds and independent new replication, not optional stopping.",
  "inferential_assumptions": "Order-statistic coverage is conditional on independent identically distributed block ratios. Random position balance does not prove this assumption; temporal load, thermal/frequency, fixed workload order can violate it. Bonferroni familywise .05 conditional on individual coverage. No unconditional causal/world-title claim.",
  "secondary": "Split/shared-half and shared-half/auto contrasts, descriptive exact sign/Holm families only. Cannot rescue failed primary gate. CPU totals descriptive; no CPU or latency noninferiority claim.",
  "intervention": "Whole-core halves sorted by SMT pair: A first four physical cores, B last four. auto=(F,F), ab=(A,B), ba=(B,A), aa=(A,A), bb=(B,B). Same L3, topology-derived masks, no singleton pins; producer and all non-target threads untouched by wrapper.",
  "decision": "If any primary bound misses margin, reject promotion on this evidence; do not add rounds to rescue. Pilot is plumbing only, excluded from 30-block confirmatory series. If all clear, require separately frozen replication; no runtime change or championship without exact-build competitor/startup/latency/correctness gates.",
  "limitations": "Shared host, no CPU isolation, no per-pass sampler, no proven residency or continuous affinity. Admission reads loadavg/CPU PSI BEFORE each whole block; records all waits, no within-block exclusion or normalization. A passing admission does not prove low per-core load during every pass. Producer unpinned, reciprocal arms not independent replicates. Boundary snapshots can alter warm state. Same selected executable and unchanged tput.py fastest of three DA1 passes 154x39. No new Ghostty metric in this experiment."
